Subject: SOP Reflective Virtual Machine

Description: A provider-independent runtime that executes compiled SOP reflection programs over inspectable semantic state while using an LLM only as a replaceable inference coprocessor.

& [FormationIdentity] is the canonical SJS runtime formation
  + [specification_uuid] is 601cdd26-e602-4235-92bc-fc76d755e050
  + [status] is minimum_reference_runtime_formation
  + [purpose] is compile SOP into an independent program that directs how an agent attends, remembers, infers, reviews, and responds
  + [runtime_name] is SOP Reflective Virtual Machine
  + [abbreviation] is SOP-RVM

& [IndependenceContract] is the separation between program and processor
  + [SOP_program] owns purpose, focus policy, history policy, inference methods, contracts, authority, review, effects, and control flow
  + [SOP_RVM] owns program state, scheduling, validation, persistence, model calls, effect gates, and transition traces
  + [inference_provider] supplies probabilistic interpretation, generation, comparison, or judgment under a bounded request
  + [host] owns process isolation, files, database, network, tools, and hardware
  = must: allow the same compiled program to run through different conforming inference providers
  = must: keep semantic state outside provider-private context
  = must: permit deterministic or tool-backed implementations of operations that do not require an LLM
  - never: let a provider silently change program, contracts, authority, or stored history

& [CompilationPipeline] is the route from articulated source to executable reflection
  + [stage_1_source] is preserved verbose or condensed SOP
  + [stage_2_parse] is syntax tree with source locations
  + [stage_3_resolve] is bound identities, contexts, libraries, types, and versions
  + [stage_4_check] is semantic, contract, effect, authority, and termination validation
  + [stage_5_lower] is normalized semantic IR
  + [stage_6_plan] is executable instruction and transition graph
  + [stage_7_package] is content-addressed program, dependencies, schemas, fixtures, and proof requirements
  = must: emit diagnostics without executing an invalid package
  = must: preserve a source map from every executable instruction to articulated SOP

& [CompiledReflectionProgram] is the independent program package
  + [program_uuid] is stable content-addressed identity
  + [purpose_contract] is intended reflective outcome
  + [subject_contract] is acceptable focus subjects
  + [instruction_graph] is compiled semantic operations and control flow
  + [history_policy] is when and how pertinent history is reviewed
  + [inference_policy] is allowed inference methods and evidence obligations
  + [review_policy] is capsule tests, independence mode, and revision bounds
  + [effect_policy] is allowed targets, authorization gates, and reversibility
  + [resource_budget] is token, time, memory, traversal, tool, and effect limits
  + [output_schema] is response, trace, uncertainty, fault, and reentry form
  + [dependency_lock] is exact semantic, library, and mapping versions
  + [proof_contract] is fixtures required for runtime admission

& [RuntimeState] is externalized inspectable agent state
  + [run_uuid] is one program execution identity
  + [program_counter] is the next instruction address
  + [semantic_state] is purpose, focus, boundary, inside, outside, frontier, evidence, uncertainty, and budget
  + [history_cursor] is the last reviewed observation position
  + [call_stack] is active functions and return points
  + [pending_effects] is proposed but uncommitted actions
  + [capsule_set] is candidate and review history
  + [status] is ready, running, waiting_for_inference, waiting_for_authority, yielded, faulted, stopped, or complete
  = must: serialize independently of model context
  = must: restore under program and dependency digest checks

& [ReflectionInstructionCycle] is how the program directs one material step
  + [step_1_load] is load current instruction, subject, state, contract, and budget
  + [step_2_recall] is perform PertinentHistoryReview
  + [step_3_project] is build a bounded ReflectionCallPacket
  + [step_4_dispatch] is execute deterministically or call an InferenceProvider
  + [step_5_receive] is parse a structured ProposedJudgment
  + [step_6_validate] is test schema, evidence, inference, constraints, authority, and budget
  + [step_7_review] is create or extend an InferenceCapsule when required
  + [step_8_transition] is accept, revise, reject, block, yield, fault, or commit an authorized effect
  + [step_9_record] is append SemanticTransition and HistoryReviewEvent
  + [step_10_advance] is select the next admissible instruction
  = must: execute this cycle until a declared terminal state

& [ReflectionCallPacket] is the complete bounded request to an inference provider
  + [call_uuid] is stable request identity
  + [operation] is the exact semantic instruction requested
  + [purpose] is current intended outcome
  + [subject_projection] is active focus and boundary
  + [history_projection] is pertinent observations, contradictions, constraints, and unresolved material
  + [evidence_projection] is available supporting material
  + [instruction_contract] is required reasoning method, output form, and prohibited behavior
  + [allowed_claim_kinds] is assertion, assumption, inference, question, uncertainty, result, or fault
  + [allowed_effects] is normally none because calls propose rather than commit
  + [budget] is maximum context and response resources
  + [output_schema] is the machine-readable response contract
  + [omission_record] is relevant content not loaded and why
  = must: provide only the context required by the current instruction

& [ProposedJudgment] is provider output awaiting runtime validation
  + [call_uuid] is the request being answered
  + [judgment_kind] is claim, assumption, relation, interpretation, inference, candidate, uncertainty, or fault
  + [content] is the proposed semantic result
  + [source_links] is evidence and history references
  + [rule_links] is declared inference or transformation rules
  + [confidence] is provider estimate separated from runtime validation
  + [state_delta_proposal] is requested attention-state change
  + [effect_proposal] is an optional uncommitted action request
  + [explanation_summary] is inspectable grounds adequate for review
  = must: remain a proposal until validated
  - never: accept free-form provider output as an authorized state transition

& [RuntimeServices] is the minimum replaceable service boundary
  + [compiler] is SOP source to compiled package
  + [state_store] is RuntimeState persistence and reentry
  + [history_store] is typed observations and semantic event history
  + [semantic_index] is identity and relation retrieval
  + [inference_adapter] is provider-specific request and result translation
  + [validator] is contract, schema, evidence, authority, and transition checking
  + [review_engine] is capsule construction and ReviewProgram execution
  + [effect_broker] is authorization and external action commitment
  + [trace_store] is append-only execution and fault events
  = must: define interfaces before choosing concrete database or model technology

& [ProviderConformance] is the minimum replaceability test
  + [structured_input] is acceptance of ReflectionCallPacket semantics
  + [structured_output] is production of ProposedJudgment schema
  + [identity_echo] is exact call and program identity preservation
  + [no_hidden_effect] is inability to commit runtime effects directly
  + [fault_visibility] is explicit refusal, truncation, invalid output, and provider failure
  + [capability_declaration] is supported context, modalities, tools, and operation kinds
  = must: compare providers through the same fixture corpus

& [MinimumManifestation] is the smallest runnable proof
  + [artifact_1] is a hand-authored machine-form semantic IR fixture without a parser
  + [artifact_2] is an in-memory RuntimeState
  + [artifact_3] is a deterministic mock InferenceProvider
  + [artifact_4] is one real model adapter after the mock passes
  + [artifact_5] is one PertinentHistoryReview
  + [artifact_6] is one candidate InferenceCapsule and ReviewReport
  + [artifact_7] is one revision and reexecution
  + [artifact_8] is an append-only transition trace
  = must: prove the execution model before building surface grammar or persistent database
  = must: remain an implementation of the existing CoreAcceptance slice rather than a new project branch

& [NeuralRelationship] is the clarified place of neural computation
  + [present_role] is replaceable inference provider behind ReflectionCallPacket
  + [later_role] is optional learned retrieval, ranking, routing, or distilled execution
  + [non_role] is canonical storage of SOP meaning, authority, contracts, or history
  = conclusion: the desired independence comes from compilation and external runtime state, not from converting SOP into weights

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable runtime formation requirement collection
  + [RVM-001] is compile SOP through syntax, resolution, checking, IR, transition graph, and package stages
  + [RVM-002] is externalize program state independently of model context
  + [RVM-003] is direct every material step through a bounded ReflectionCallPacket
  + [RVM-004] is treat provider output as a proposal requiring validation
  + [RVM-005] is make inference providers replaceable and effects brokered
  + [RVM-006] is integrate pertinent history, inference capsules, review, revision, and replay
  + [RVM-007] is prove the runtime with machine-form fixtures and a mock provider before parser or database expansion

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the reflective virtual machine formation trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is SOP compiled into an independent reflective program executed over external semantic state
  + [fold_2_boundary] is program and runtime authority outside the model; bounded probabilistic inference inside provider calls
  + [fold_3_data_design] is source, IR, package, state, call packet, proposed judgment, transition, capsule, effect, and trace identity
  + [fold_4_governance] is provider replaceability, source maps, validation, effect brokering, digest-bound reentry, and proof admission
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is compile once and repeatedly load, recall, project, dispatch, receive, validate, review, transition, record, and advance
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is prompt-owned state, provider-owned authority, free-form transition, hidden effect, parser-first expansion, and premature database choice
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is minimum machine-form runtime proof defined as the current CoreAcceptance implementation path

